# Project Architecture Rules

This project is a local Django application that will later be wrapped inside a Windows desktop application using PySide6 and Qt WebEngine.

The current phase is Django prototype development only.

Do NOT implement PySide6, Qt WebEngine, or PyInstaller unless explicitly requested.

## Django

Use:

- Python
- Django
- SQLite
- Django Templates
- HTML
- CSS
- Minimal vanilla JavaScript

Do not introduce:

- React
- Vue
- Angular
- Node.js frontend frameworks
- Django REST Framework
- GraphQL

unless explicitly requested.

## Django Apps

The project should contain only these two Django apps:

- accounts
- notes

Do not create additional Django apps unless explicitly requested.

## Architecture

Keep business logic inside Django.

Use:

- Django ORM
- Django Forms
- Django Authentication
- Django URL routing
- Django Templates

Do not unnecessarily introduce additional architectural layers.

## Desktop Compatibility

The Django application must remain suitable for future execution inside:

PySide6
→ Qt WebEngine
→ Windows executable

Avoid cloud dependencies and external services.

Do not implement PyInstaller-specific logic during the current prototype phase.

## Development

Work incrementally.

Inspect existing files before editing them.

Do not rewrite functioning code unnecessarily.

Do not implement future features unless explicitly requested.